    "content": "Hot take: every social app should ship an “explain this thread” button that runs on the user’s own inference — not the app’s backend.\n\nKeys and model choice stay with the user. The app just passes the note + replies as context.\n\nIf your client can’t do that without asking me for an OpenAI key, it’s doing it wrong.",
    "created_at": 1735689600
  },
